---
title: "Machine Blueprint Reading"
code: "DRF-160"
category: "drafting"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Introduces interpreting of various blueprints and working drawings. Applies basic principles and techniques such as visualization of an object, orthographic projection, technical sketching and drafting terminology. Requires outside preparation. Lecture 3 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
